    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_02caa76a58265a686a1f5036fa6e81252ec70932aebc150557c9f69bad2bfb2a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a single proof spine in which critical-line derivative symmetry selects an auxiliary η whose real-part zeros can be lower-bounded by argument change; factoring η through H then replaces its derivative combination by the polynomial differential transform V; the argument principle, mollification, Littlewood's lemma, and arithmetic-geometric mean turn that count into a mollified second moment; and the stated mean-value theorem supplies the analytic input for that moment when θ<4/7.",
