    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ad2d2edfb7d6c3cf42c86d4dee132ff5521f121b69c8ba34d727f9271bcb2674",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source evaluates the derivative-bearing target mean by first encoding derivatives in two small shifts and recovering them by Cauchy differentiation, then splitting the shifted proposition into a discrete mollifier-coefficient calculation and an analytic calculation of g. In the analytic branch, functional equations and contour splitting produce smoothed off-diagonal sums; Estermann Mellin duality decomposes them into main, residual, and error pieces; and localization near the singular point evaluates the two main pieces by the same residue contribution.",
